WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.169
-Our first guests tonight
are the father/son duo

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.238
you know from shows
like "9-1-1: Lone Star,"

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.505
"The Grinder"
and "The Lowe Files."

00:00:06.505 --> 00:00:09.075
They co-created
and star in "Unstable,"

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.543
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.612
Let's take a look.
-Let's talk about us.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.280
-Us?
-I'm worried about us.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.316
-Are we an "us"? I've never
thought of us as an "us."

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.351
-Exactly. Since you've been
here, you've made friends.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.321
That's great. But we haven't
spent much time together.

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.989
-Mm-hmm.
Because at work, you're my boss.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.090
And at home, you're my dad.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.925
And everybody else is just
a normal friend.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:30.196
-Yes. So let's go somewhere
where we're not father/son

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.932
or boss/employee.
Just friends.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.901
-Oh, my God. Are you going to
make me jump out of an airplane

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.135
strapped face-to-face with you
again?

00:00:36.135 --> 00:00:37.670
Because that was terrible.
-Well, I loved it.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.271
And I'm the one
who got vomited on.

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:43.209
-Please welcome to the show Rob
and John Owen Lowe, everyone.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.977
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.977 --> 00:01:05.498 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.668
Welcome to the show, gentlemen.
This is very exciting for me.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.636
-It's very exciting for me
to sit

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:13.172
in the least important position
in the studio.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.774
-There you go.
-I knew he was going

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.008
to say something about this.
-Yeah, he was going to

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:17.744
jump right in.
And I noticed he pointed there.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:19.712
He wanted you to sit there
and then he was going

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.481
to be like, "Woe is me."
-Well, he wanted it

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.082
to make it seem like it was
his decision.

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:24.317
-That's exactly right.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.552
-You were going to sit here
no matter what?

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.787
-That's what I want
everyone else to know.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.022
But yes.
-So you are --

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:32.458
You are playing father/son
in this show.

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.227
You are not playing
this father/son.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:36.996
But it does seem to be
a heightened version

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.864
of your reality.
Is that fair?

00:01:38.864 --> 00:01:42.268
-It is. I think that Rob
is dangerously close

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.670
to as insane as his character
is on the show.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.505
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:48.274
-But it's -- yeah, it's --

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.376
I mean, you want
to defend yourself slightly?

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.078
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.879
-Yes.

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:58.050
What happened was John Owen
would troll me mercilessly.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.618
And I think the last time I was
on the show --

00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:03.123
-I was going to say we
dove deep into the fact

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.757
that you got trolled hard
by John Owen.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.994
-And thank you then
for making this show happen

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:10.596
because it caught on
and people kind of liked it.

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:12.031
And we were like,
"Maybe there's a show there."

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.566
And that's how we came up
with the idea.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:16.202
-And so this premise, again,
you are not Rob Lowe the actor,

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.604
and you are not his son,
but you are --

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.172
I mean, is it safe
to say -- and again,

00:02:20.172 --> 00:02:21.774
correct me
if I offend your father

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:25.078
in any way -- an egomaniac?
Maybe a bit of an egomaniac?

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:29.582
-Yeah. No, I mean, yes. A bit?
Yeah.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:34.621
I mean, and to be clear,
this is like not a bit.

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.722
We leave here and get
in the car together

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:39.125
and it's straight to the car
mirror and like,

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.360
"how do I look" and...
-Gotcha.

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.195
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:45.297
-This is authentic.
-Now, see, I would --

00:02:45.297 --> 00:02:47.900
And again, you're going to be
less a part of this.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.402
-Okay.
-Thank God.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.303
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.304
-Because I would have thought --

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.805
And again, I've met your dad.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.708
Your dad is a very cool person
when you meet him in real life.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.309
And I would have thought
he was a very cool dad.

00:02:57.309 --> 00:02:58.844
But based
on your social media,

00:02:58.844 --> 00:03:01.147
I've been completely disabused
of that notion.

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:02.849
-First of all,
I'm glad to hear that. Yeah.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.383
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:08.320
Look, he is cool. I will
begrudgingly admit that --

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.257
Well, I don't know about cool,
but he's a good dad.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.392
-He's handsome.
-Yeah, well, yeah.

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:15.794
[ Laughter ]
Sure.

00:03:15.794 --> 00:03:18.531
He's a good dad.
But he's -- You...

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.431
-Yes.
-...are...

00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:21.434
-Yes.
-...fairly insane.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.902
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:27.106
And, you know, I like to say
a benevolent narcissist, right?

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.808
So yes.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.210
-Benevolent.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.312
-Well, now, Rob,
I have to say again,

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:34.847
I have a couple
of boys of my own.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.615
I can't even imagine
how wonderful it must be

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:37.717
to be on set together.

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:39.051
And especially,
I should note as well,

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:42.221
this show has been incredibly
well received so far.

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:44.157
Are you just so happy
and proud every day?

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.559
-It's pretty -- It's really
special because, I mean,

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:49.328
you're a generation
behind me with your kids,

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:52.198
but they'll get to a point where
they don't need you anymore

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.132
and they're off in their lives

00:03:54.132 --> 00:03:57.503
and you have to figure out ways
to spend time with them.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.439
-Yeah.
-And that's what we have done.

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:02.975
-Yes.
-And you obviously must love

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:04.577
your son John because, again,
like I said,

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:07.246
he's been very hard on you.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:09.715
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:12.351
This is one where
you wrote, Rob,

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:14.453
you wrote "Who wore it best?"

00:04:14.453 --> 00:04:16.455
-I thought it was funny.
See, I'm doing

00:04:16.455 --> 00:04:19.859
the Angelina Jolie leg.
-And first comment was John here

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:22.194
"Why did you start using
Instagram freely again?

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:23.996
Go back to the podcast posts."

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:26.098
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:28.567
-That was a good one.
I'm proud of that one.

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:31.337
-This is again, this is
all him commenting on you.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.039
So there are you on the boat.
And now again, Rob,

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:34.273
you tried to be funny here.
"Unreal.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:36.275
This drug-smuggling boat
landed on our beach

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:37.776
in the middle of the night.
Happy Labor Day."

00:04:37.776 --> 00:04:39.645
-True.
-John wrote,

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:41.146
"We need to start
teaching our parents

00:04:41.146 --> 00:04:42.782
Internet literacy and decorum."

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.651
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:47.686
-Can I just quickly
just say that that's real?

00:04:47.686 --> 00:04:50.489
That boat washed up
and it was like a crime scene

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:52.325
and he thought
he was important enough

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.892
that he could just go there

00:04:53.892 --> 00:04:58.398
and start touching things,
like a live crime scene,

00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:01.834
and then post about it
on Instagram.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:06.372
And so it's kind of a bit,
but it's also very real.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:09.675
-You're trying to like --
It's an intervention of a sort.

00:05:09.675 --> 00:05:11.411
-At a certain point
you'd think he'd notice,

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.846
but I just get to keep going
because he hasn't noticed yet.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:16.149
-This is really the best one.
It's the Oscars.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:17.282
-Yeah.

00:05:17.282 --> 00:05:19.251
-You once famously
performed the Oscars.

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:20.653
-Oh, yes. Oh, yes.
-Yeah.

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:22.187
Maybe the kids
don't remember it.

00:05:22.187 --> 00:05:23.989
-Well, they will now!

00:05:23.989 --> 00:05:26.425
-So you did a song and dance
with Snow White.

00:05:26.425 --> 00:05:29.228
-Yes, I did.
-And this is the photo

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:30.596
that John put up that says,

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:33.332
"Congrats to all the Oscar
winners, and to the losers,

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:35.268
you still never did this."

00:05:35.268 --> 00:05:38.203
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.203 --> 00:05:42.441
-That -- I was. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:44.143
That one was mean.

00:05:46.178 --> 00:05:48.381
That one maybe was too mean.
-No, I don't think --

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:51.784
Look, I'm good. The meaner,
the better. I can take it.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.152
-You're a good sport.
-Thank you.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:55.621
-Now, the other thing, though,
is, Rob, is it accurate

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:59.258
that John did not
grow up watching your films?

00:05:59.258 --> 00:06:00.392
-Ask him.

00:06:00.392 --> 00:06:01.727
-Did you watch any of
your dad's movies?

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:03.029
Oh, no, no, no. Ask him about
your favorite

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.130
"West Wing" moment.
-Okay.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.899
What's your favorite "West Wing"
moment?

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:09.568
-I don't have one
'cause I've never seen it.

00:06:09.568 --> 00:06:11.370
-You never watched
"The West Wing"?

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:12.838
-I will say this much.

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:15.340
Aaron Sorkin and the rest of the
cast, incredibly talented.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:19.278
-Okay now.
-I'm sure they're great.

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:22.849
I bet that show is phenomenal,
but I've never seen it.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.016
-He's actually not kidding.

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.918
-Now, how does
that make you feel?

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:28.154
-Sad and lonely.
-And lonely.

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:29.455
You would feel
like that either way.

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.156
-I guess so
you realize -- And again now,

00:06:31.156 --> 00:06:33.259
I don't want to turn this on you
because, you know,

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:36.162
we've talked about your dad's
imperfections a great deal here.

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:38.831
I got to say, John, the fact
that you will only watch

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:41.033
one of your dad's shows
that you're in...

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:43.269
-Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.269 --> 00:06:45.270
-You know, I got to be honest,
it's a real, like,

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.639
son of Rob Lowe thing to do.
-Look.

00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:49.709
[ Laughter ]
That is totally fair.

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:51.644
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:54.113
-That's valid. That's valid.

00:06:54.113 --> 00:06:55.314
I watched "Parks and Rec."

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:57.450
I watched that
before he went on it and then...

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.718
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:00.887
...continued to watch it.

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:02.521
-Oh, that's nice.
-Yes.

00:07:02.521 --> 00:07:03.689
-What about on set?

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.591
Because you you have
less of a background.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:08.093
I know you're a writer,
but on camera,

00:07:08.093 --> 00:07:11.630
this show was a bit of a --
it's a big deal.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:14.099
Was it helpful to have your dad
on set as your costar?

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:15.601
-It was.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.970
But he...

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:21.574
He's difficult at times.
I would say that...

00:07:21.574 --> 00:07:23.876
There was this one moment --
I'll share this one moment

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:26.144
because it was sweet
but also disturbing,

00:07:26.144 --> 00:07:29.715
which was that
the first day of shooting,

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:32.919
it's the first shot
and I'm a little nervous.

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:37.022
I haven't been -- I hadn't had
that much responsibility on set.

00:07:37.022 --> 00:07:38.791
And so it's like
I got to get on my mark.

00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:40.893
We're about to roll.
And right before we roll,

00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:43.862
you started to ramble about
how the mark was wrong

00:07:43.862 --> 00:07:45.397
and how someone was going
to cross in front of me

00:07:45.397 --> 00:07:47.500
and my hair looked off

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.235
and maybe my chin
wasn't chiseled enough

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:50.603
and whatever it was.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:52.204
And it got me to this place

00:07:52.204 --> 00:07:54.473
where I was very frustrated
and very anxious.

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:57.343
And then they called action,
and it was what my character

00:07:57.343 --> 00:07:59.344
was supposed to be doing
in that moment.

00:07:59.344 --> 00:08:00.980
And I thought to myself
afterwards, I'm like,

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.749
"Damn it, did he just, like,
Miyagi me or something?"

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:05.117
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.117 --> 00:08:09.088
But I don't want to give him
that much credit, so...

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:11.723
-Very, very well played, Dad.

00:08:11.723 --> 00:08:14.960
Very impressive.
It's a wonderful show.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:17.362
And it is just so delightful
to see you guys here in person.

00:08:17.362 --> 00:08:18.397
Thanks so much
for making the time.

00:08:18.397 --> 00:08:20.132
-Thank you.
-Thank you for having us.

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:23.135
-The Lowes, Rob and John Owen,
everybody.

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:25.438
"Unstable" streaming now
on Netflix.

00:08:25.438 --> 00:08:27.206
We'll be right back with
Judd Winick.

